     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Something that has just happened",
     "texto": [
      "To say something has just happened, use **venir** in the present + **de** + infinitive: **Je viens de finir** (I've just finished).",
      "The main verb stays in the infinitive: **Elle vient de rentrer**, **Nous venons de manger**.",
      "The present tense of **venir** is irregular; look at the forms in the table."
